    "cost_closing_html":  "About \u003cstrong\u003e$4.24 a bowl\u003c/strong\u003e (at everyday cost) for a baked pasta dish the casual Italian places list at $15. The gnocchi never even gets boiled separately, so you save on dishes too.",
    "shop_smart":  ["Shelf-stable gnocchi is cheap by the pack here and cooks straight in the sauce, no boiling pot, no waste.","The 93/7 beef is over half the batch cost. Time this recipe to the 4 lb pack sale and the per-bowl price drops fast.","Jarred marinara in four store-brand jars beats making sauce from canned tomatoes once you count the herbs, oil, and simmer time."],
    "make_it":  [
                    "Weigh your empty mixing pot and write the number down for portioning later.",
                    "Heat the oven to 400F. In a big oven-safe pot, brown the ground beef with the diced onion, breaking it up as it cooks, until no pink remains.",
                    "Add the garlic and Italian seasoning and cook 1 minute, then season with salt and black pepper.",
                    "Pour in the marinara sauce with a splash of water, bring it to a simmer, and stir in the uncooked gnocchi. Simmer 3 to 4 minutes, stirring so nothing sticks.",
                    "Dollop the ricotta over the top and scatter on the mozzarella.",
                    "Bake 15 to 20 minutes until the cheese is melted and the sauce bubbles at the edges. Rest 5 minutes.",
                    "Portion evenly into 14 containers."
